"""
Return the terminal current density of the device in amperes per square metre, taking the sign convention in which a current driven out of the device by the built-in field is negative. Raise ValueError if the total current is not independent of position to within one part in a thousand.

Each carrier current varies across the layer, because generation and recombination move carriers between the two species. Their sum does not, and that is the terminal current. Checking that the sum really is flat is the sharpest available test that the two continuity equations were discretised consistently with one another, because an error in either one leaves the sum sloping while each equation on its own still appears to be solved.

Returns
-------
float, in amperes per square metre
"""

